				if accepted[i] != offer[i] {
					break
				}
			}
			if i == len(accepted) {
				return offer
			}

When an offered format is a proper prefix of the accepted format (e.g. Accept: "text/html" and offered "text"), `offer[i]` is indexed past the end of `offer` and the library panics with "index out of range". Fix by bounding the loop: `for ; i < len(accepted) && i < len(offer); i++ {` — change nothing else in the function.

